  "question": "If $R$ is the region bounded by $y = x^2$, $y = 4$, and $x=1$, then the area of $R$ is:",
  "answeroption": "A",
  "explanation": "Solve $x^2=4 \\Rightarrow x=2$.<br /><br />Between $1$ and $2$, upper curve $=4$, lower $=x^2$.<br /><br />Area $=\\int_{1}^{2}(4-x^2)dx$.<br /><br />Hence option A is correct.",
  "explanation_image": [],
  "options": {
    "A": "$\\int_{1}^{2} (4-x^2) dx$",
    "B": "$\\int_{-2}^{1} (4-x^2) dx$",
    "C": "$\\int_{1}^{2} (x^2-4) dx$",
    "D": "$\\int_{1}^{2} (x^2+4) dx$"
  },
